      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 89, sold as Sedum 'Autumn Joy' (a hybrid); this entry is the species the list names. Pages: NC State and MBG (two Plant Finder pages cached; the second is cultivar 'Autumn Fire', not cited). No RHS or Clemson page; the ASPCA sedum and hylotelephium pages returned an empty soft 404, so there is no pet source: pets read 'not assessed'. Toxicity: NC State low severity for people, alkaloids sedine and sedamine, symptoms unknown but possibly gastrointestinal, contact dermatitis no; the symptom words are the agent's mapping. Hardiness left empty (MBG USDA 3 to 9; no RHS page read). Low creeping sedums (Sedum acre, S. album) are other plants. Watering: both pages say drought tolerant, dry to medium, well-drained soil; let_fully_dry for a pot is the agent's mapping and 10 days a guess. Size: NC State and MBG 30 to 60 cm tall and wide. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
